WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.639 --> 00:00:03.280
There’s a temptation

00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:06.000
to withdraw nationally

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.280
each time we are tested.

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:10.759
However, nothing is more futile

00:00:10.759 --> 00:00:12.680
than trying to save only ourselves.

00:00:13.319 --> 00:00:16.360
Nobody takes leaving their homeland lightly,

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:19.119
not even those who come for economic reasons.

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:28.519
Since the Second World War,

00:00:28.519 --> 00:00:30.720
there have never been as many displaced people as today,

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:31.439
around 60 million.

00:00:32.039 --> 00:00:35.839
It's a humanitarian crisis we're facing,

00:00:35.839 --> 00:00:39.280
with an influx of refugees.

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:41.200
With each crisis,

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:44.200
fears are manifested.

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:46.680
You have to live with fear,

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:50.839
but you must not live dominated by fear.

00:00:50.839 --> 00:00:52.680
Isolation and closure 

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:55.839
in the internet age are an illusion.

00:00:55.839 --> 00:00:58.000
No problems would be solved

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:01.800
but additional serious problems would arise

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:04.479
because the commitment to our values 

00:01:04.479 --> 00:01:08.439
and thus our identity would be lost.

00:01:08.439 --> 00:01:10.200
If we disregard that,

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:11.879
we are betraying ourselves.

00:01:11.879 --> 00:01:14.400
Nothing more and nothing less.

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:23.079
Europe was slow to understand

00:01:23.079 --> 00:01:25.560
that the tragedies in the Middle East or in Africa

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:29.119
would not be without consequences.

00:01:29.119 --> 00:01:30.920
Europe has not measured the hope

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:33.000
that it evokes

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:34.720
and will long continue to evoke.

00:01:35.239 --> 00:01:39.280
We must focus our foreign and development policy

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:43.360
much more on solving conflicts 

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:46.239
and combatting what causes people to leave.

00:01:52.639 --> 00:01:54.560
Only together will we succeed in achieving a fair

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:56.759
and appropriate distribution of refugees

00:01:56.759 --> 00:01:59.280
across all member states.

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:00.319
Let's face it,

00:02:00.319 --> 00:02:05.360
the Dublin procedure in its current form is obsolete.

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:08.920
Calling into question the free movement of people

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:11.439
by returning to internal borders

00:02:11.439 --> 00:02:13.759
would be a tragic mistake.

00:02:13.759 --> 00:02:15.959
But claiming...

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:24.280
But claiming that the Schengen area, in its current form,

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:28.360
makes it possible to counter the pressure on its external borders

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:30.360
would be another mistake.

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:35.560
Less than twenty-six years ago,

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:38.319
before leaving office,

00:02:38.319 --> 00:02:41.479
François Mitterrand came to speak at the European Parliament.

00:02:41.479 --> 00:02:44.039
He said nationalism is war.

00:02:44.039 --> 00:02:46.959
His warning still applies today.

00:02:53.239 --> 00:02:56.680
The debate is not between less Europe and more Europe.

00:02:56.680 --> 00:02:58.759
It is between the affirmation of Europe

00:02:58.759 --> 00:03:00.479
or the end of Europe.

00:03:00.479 --> 00:03:01.639
Yes, the end of Europe,

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:04.600
that is to say the return to national borders.

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:15.159
More than ever, we need the courage and cohesion

00:03:15.159 --> 00:03:20.280
that Europe has always shown when it matters most,

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:22.759
and Germany and France are ready for it.

00:03:22.759 --> 00:03:25.600
Let us work on this together

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:28.119
- as Helmut Kohl proposed

00:03:28.119 --> 00:03:29.759
here in the European Parliament in 1989

00:03:29.759 --> 00:03:33.720
with a view to the changes in Central and Eastern Europe

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:35.400
- and I quote him:

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:38.000
“With wisdom and a sense of proportion,

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:41.759
with ingenuity and flexibility.” Thank you.

